 *
 * Context:
 * An e-commerce platform has different types of users, each
 * having specific roles and responsibilities. However, all
 * users share some common properties and behaviors.
 *
 * Common Attributes:
 * - username
 * - email
 *
 * Common Behavior:
 * - login()
 *
 * User Types:
 * 1. AdminUser
 *    - Manages products
 *    - Manages sellers and customers
 *    - Views reports and analytics
 *
 * 2. SellerUser
 *    - Adds new products
 *    - Updates product information
 *    - Manages inventory
 *    - Views customer orders
 *
 * 3. RegularUser (Customer)
 *    - Browses products
 *    - Adds products to cart
 *    - Places orders
 *    - Tracks order status
 *
 * OOP Concept Used:
 * The Users class acts as the Parent (Superclass), while
 * AdminUser, SellerUser, and RegularUser inherit from it,
 * reusing common properties and methods while implementing
 * their own specialized functionalities.
 * ==========================================================
